            "bit width — Number of bits in a representation.",
            "two's complement — Fixed-width signed binary format.",
            "mantissa — Signed fractional significant component.",
            "exponent — Power-of-two scaling value.",
            "precision — Number of significant digits retained."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Respect the bit width",
          "text": "Write positive 5 using exactly eight bits."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Invert then add one",
          "text": "The result is 11111011₂, representing −5 in 8-bit two's complement."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Interpret floating-point differently",
          "text": "0.1100₂ is fractional 0.75; multiplying by 2³ gives 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "title": "Worked example · Predict",
          "text": "Write 00001010 for +10 and invert to 11110101."
        },
